  <main_text>
    <l n="1">sufficere, gladium à quopiam</l>
    <l n="2">stringi, nisi etiam accesserit</l>
    <l n="3">percussio, saltem adfuerit co-</l>
    <l n="4">natus percutiendi manifestatus</l>
    <l n="5">aliquo indicio. Ut ita de in-</l>
    <l n="6">tentione &amp; animo aggressoris</l>
    <l n="7">judici magis constare possit,</l>
    <l n="8">adeoque de absolutione vel</l>
    <l n="9">condemnatione faciendâ, li-</l>
    <l n="10">quere. Ut vero alicui permis-</l>
    <l n="11">sum sit se tueri, sufficit eum in</l>
    <l n="12">dubio vitæ discrimine consti-</l>
    <l n="13">tutum esse. Quod tunc immi-</l>
    <l n="14">nere judicatur, cum aliquis</l>
    <l n="15">eundem, armatum manu, licet</l>
    <l n="16">nondum percusserit, aggredi-</l>
    <l n="17">tur. Terror quippe armorum</l>
    <l n="18">inducit vitæ discrimen.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Neque obstat 3. Quod de</l>
    <l n="20">jure dicatur illatam vim esse</l>
    <l n="21">propulsandam. Neque censea-</l>
    <l n="22">tur illata, quæ est inferenda.</l>
    <l n="23">Respondeo enim satis super-</l>
    <l n="24">que vim alicui illatam censeri,</l>
    <l n="25">si adversarius stricto mucrone</l>
    <l n="26">aliquem aggrediatur, licet</l>
